/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate29_vp_methylTertPentylEther -- the vapour pressure of methylTertPentylEther, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  methylTertPentylEther`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je101250d                21 pts  313.44-359.95 K  Mejia; Segura; Cartes
      10.1021/je0255980                11 pts  274.2-307.8 K  Verevkin; Krasnykh; Vasiltsova; Heintz
      10.1021/je049867t                11 pts  298.02-355.64 K  Vorenberg; Raal; Ramjugernath
      10.1021/je901026b                 5 pts  318.13-338.28 K  Bernatova; Pavlicek; Wichterle
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.06.017: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.10.024: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je200215d: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je101250d (21 pts, 313.44-359.95 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je0255980 (11 pts,
  274.2-307.8 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 7.8 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 11 points (7.75 to 7.77 %, mean 7.764 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 359.51 K lies INSIDE the measured span 274.2-359.95 K: the held-out verdict is the test there, no further condition.

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.240937 - 1366.2891/(T + -36.8588),
  in-sample R2 0.999996 over 21 points, 313.44-359.95 K. HELD OUT: 11
  points, AAD 9.9414 % against the band 7.8 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 359.46 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 9.941 % against the band 7.8 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  methylTertPentylEther;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylTertPentylEther-vapourPressure-je101250d.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je101250d"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylTertPentylEther-vapourPressure-je0255980.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je0255980"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  7.8 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 11 points (7.75 to 7.77 %, mean 7.764 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
